===  E5-c018 L01
  back OLD: 'No. Proposition 2.4 gives basket A, with P^L = 5/4 above P^P = 27/23, and basket B, with P^L = 11/10 below P^P = 19/10. Which index is closer to a true cost of living is a separate question that Proposition 2.4 does not settle.'
  back NEW: 'No. Under (A1) of Proposition 2.4 (one two-good basket with positive prices and quantities), basket B gives P^L = 11/10 below P^P = 19/10, so the Laspeyres index is the smaller one there. Which index is closer to a true cost of living is a separate question that Proposition 2.4 does not settle.'
===  E5-c019 L01
  back OLD: 'No. At a 25 percent simple inflation rate the log rate is ln 1.25 = 0.223144, which is 0.026856 lower. The gap is small at low rates and grows with the rate, as Lab 1 Part C prints for x = 0.01, 0.05 and 0.25.'
  back NEW: 'No. Proposition 2.5 holds for every x > -1. At a 25 percent simple inflation rate the log rate is ln 1.25 = 0.223144, which is 0.026856 lower. The gap is small at low rates and grows with the rate, as Lab 1 Part C gives for x = 0.01, 0.05 and 0.25.'
