===  E5-c031 L02
  back OLD: "Under Assumption 1.3, the residual computed with the economy's own alpha satisfies Res(t) = ΔlnA(t) for every t from 1 to H (Theorem 2.3). The lesson says the economy's own alpha is needed in general, and that the identity also holds for every alpha when capital and labour grow at the same rate in every period (Problem P2)."
  back NEW: "Under Assumption 1.3, the residual computed with the economy's own alpha satisfies Res(t) = ΔlnA(t) for every t from 1 to H (Theorem 2.3). The economy's own alpha is needed in general, and the identity also holds for every alpha when capital and labour grow at the same rate in every period (Problem P2)."
