===  E5-c038 L03
  back OLD: 'Divide K(t+1) = (1 - delta) K(t) + s K(t)^alpha L(t)^(1 - alpha) by L(t+1) = (1 + n) L(t). This gives k(t+1) = (s k(t)^alpha + (1 - delta) k(t))/(1 + n). The step uses only the production function, the labour growth rule and the definitions (Derivation 1.2).'
  back NEW: 'Divide K(t+1) = (1 - delta) K(t) + s K(t)^alpha L(t)^(1 - alpha) by L(t+1) = (1 + n) L(t). This gives k(t+1) = (s k(t)^alpha + (1 - delta) k(t))/(1 + n).'
  basis OLD: 'Derivation 1.2 (proof on page)'
  basis NEW: 'Derivation 1.2'
